# Project Context

## What is ThriveSparrow?

ThriveSparrow is a **multi-tenant HR and employee engagement platform**. It covers employee engagement surveys (Pulse, eNPS, Exit), 360-degree performance feedback, OKRs/goals, employee recognition (Kudos/awards), 1:1 meetings, action plans, and an employee directory. It integrates with Slack, Teams, Google Workspace, and Outlook.

This repo is the **E2E UI automation project** for ThriveSparrow, using Playwright + JavaScript ES modules with the Page Object Model pattern.

## Application Modules Under Test

| Module | Product Area | What It Does |
|---|---|---|
| **Engage** | Surveys | Pulse, eNPS, and Exit surveys — creation, builder, config, distribution, launch, attendance, reports (overview, heatmap, responses, conversations) |
| **Performance/360** | Feedback | 360-degree feedback surveys — scales, roles, multi-level approval, CSV-link attendance, PDF reports, team analytics |
| **Goals** | OKRs | Objectives and Key Results — goal cycles, company/team/individual goals, key result progress tracking |
| **Kudos** | Recognition | Highfives, awards (fixed/variable points), multi-level approval workflows, leaderboard |
| **People** | HR Directory | Employee CRUD, departments, job titles, smart lists, guests, CSV/HRIS import, custom properties, profiles |
| **Core** | Platform | Account creation, signup verification, portal branding, billing |
| **Action Plans** | Follow-up | Action plans generated from Engage and Performance report insights — assignees, due dates |
| **Actionables** | Task Hub | Employee-facing pending tasks — surveys to attend, cutoff time enforcement |
| **OneOnOne (1:1)** | Meetings | Manager-employee meetings — agenda, action items, notes, Google Calendar sync |
| **Survey List** | Shared | Survey listing shared across Engage and Performance — search, filter, question banks |

## Test Framework Tech Stack

| Component | Technology |
|---|---|
| Test runner | Playwright Test |
| Language | JavaScript (ES modules — `import`/`export`) |
| Design pattern | Page Object Model via `POManager` |
| UI actions | `PwActions` wrapper (never raw Playwright methods) |
| Assertions | Playwright `expect` with mandatory failure messages |
| Reporting | Allure |
| Test data | `faker` + `Date.now()` for uniqueness |
| Visual testing | `PwActions.visualTestComparison()` |
| CI | Bitbucket Pipelines + Jenkins |

## Framework Architecture

```
thrivePage (Playwright page + auto-login/logout fixture)
    │
    ├── POManager ─── getXxxPage() ─── Page Object (locators + methods)
    │                                       │
    │                                       └── PwActions (click, fill, wait, navigate)
    │                                              │
    │                                              └── Playwright API (browser automation)
    │
    ├── EntityIds ─── State sharing between test steps (surveyId, cookie, etc.)
    │
    ├── CommonPageFunctions ─── Cross-module utilities (navigation, search, downloads)
    │
    └── Allure ─── Step reporting, attachments, failure artifacts
```

- **`thrivePage`** — Playwright `page` with auto-login before each test, auto-logout after, network monitoring, and failure artifacts (screenshot, video, trace). Defined in `TSAP/Fixtures/application-setup.js`.
- **`POManager`** — Single entry point for all page objects. Never instantiate page classes directly.
- **`PwActions`** — Static wrapper over Playwright methods. All UI interactions must go through it.
- **`EntityIds`** — Singleton for sharing state (IDs, URLs, cookies) between test steps within a test.

## Project Structure

```
TSAP/
├── Pages/              # Page objects organized by module (locators + interaction methods)
│   └── POManager.js    # Central registry — always use this to get page objects
├── Tests/
│   ├── WebApp_Testing/ # E2E regression specs, one folder per module
│   └── Visual_Testing/ # Visual regression specs
├── Data/               # Environment config, constants, test files, YAML data
├── Fixtures/           # thrivePage fixture (login/logout, network monitor, artifacts)
├── Shared_Functions/   # Cross-page utilities, EntityIds, calculations
└── Scripts/            # CI/CD scripts (reports, sharding, uploads)
```

## Common Commands

```bash
# Run all tests (QA environment)
npm run test

# Run specific test file
npx cross-env ENV=qa npx playwright test path/to/test.spec.js

# Run headed (visible browser)
npx cross-env ENV=qa npx playwright test --headed path/to/test.spec.js

# Run smoke tests
npm run smoke

# Run production sanity
npm run productionSanity

# Rerun last failed tests
npm run rerun-last-failed-test

# Playwright UI mode (interactive)
npm run ui-mode

# Generate Allure report
npm run allure_report

# View Allure report
npm run serve_allure_report

# View Playwright HTML report
npm run report
```

## Environment Configuration

Tests use `.env` to select the target environment. `Environment.json` holds per-environment config (URLs, credentials, feature flags). The `envDetails` object exports the active environment's config:

```javascript
import { envDetails } from "../../Data/test-data.js";
const baseUrl = envDetails.url;
const adminEmail = envDetails.adminEmail;
```

Key `.env` variables: `ENV` (environment name), `WORKERS` (parallel workers), `RETRIES` (retry count), `TOTAL_SHARDS` / `CURRENT_SHARD` (CI sharding).

## Domain Knowledge for Test Generation

- **Engage surveys** require a keyword in the name (`"pulse"`, `"engage"`, `"exit"`) for `createNewSurvey()` to select the correct type.
- **360 surveys** use CSV-link attendance and have an approver workflow before subjects see reports.
- **Goals** are hierarchical (company > team > individual) and belong to goal cycles.
- **Kudos awards** support multi-level approval and fixed/variable point values.
- **People** data feeds all other modules — employees created here become survey participants, goal assignees, etc.
- **Action Plans** require a full survey lifecycle (create, build, distribute, launch, attend) before they can be created from reports.
- **Actionables** show pending surveys to employees — tests verify appearance and cutoff time enforcement.
